{
  "uid": "cloudpipe-failure-triage",
  "title": "CloudPipe — Failure Triage",
  "description": "Failed and skipped pipeline steps with their category and reason, from step_outcomes. Skipped is a normal outcome, not a problem — see the dashboard notes.",
  "tags": [
    "cloudpipe",
    "failures",
    "operations"
  ],
  "links": [
    {
      "type": "dashboards",
      "title": "CloudPipe dashboards",
      "tags": [
        "cloudpipe"
      ],
      "asDropdown": true,
      "icon": "external link",
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": true,
      "targetBlank": false
    }
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "5m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-7d",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 900,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 9,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### 🔧 What went wrong, and where\n\nEvery pipeline step records its own outcome, per participant and per scan. This dashboard shows the two non-successful ones.\n\n**Skipped is normal.** A step is skipped when its output already exists — reprocessing a participant whose anatomical was already done skips the whole anatomical branch on purpose. A high skip count usually means work was *saved*, not lost.\n\n**Failed needs a person.** `failure_category` groups causes; `upstream_failed_step` tells you when a step failed only because something before it did — fix the root step, not the symptom.\n\n**History is kept, not replaced.** Records are per workflow attempt, so a failure that has since been fixed by reprocessing still appears here. Narrow the time range to the batch you care about."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Participants affected",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 9,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 5,
        "h": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "cloudpipe-athena",
        "type": "grafana-athena-datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "table",
          "format": 1,
          "connectionArgs": {
            "catalog": "__default",
            "database": "__default",
            "region": "__default"
          },
          "rawSQL": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT subject) AS failed_subjects FROM cloudpipe_metrics.step_outcomes WHERE status = 'failed' AND from_iso8601_timestamp(recorded_at) BETWEEN $__timeFrom() AND $__timeTo() AND CAST(dt AS DATE) BETWEEN CAST($__timeFrom() AS DATE) AND CAST($__timeTo() AS DATE)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "red"
          }
        }
      },
      "description": "Distinct participants with at least one failed step in range. Reprocessed-and-since-fixed participants still count while their failed attempt is in the window.",
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value",
        "justifyMode": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Failed steps",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 14,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 5,
        "h": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "cloudpipe-athena",
        "type": "grafana-athena-datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "table",
          "format": 1,
          "connectionArgs": {
            "catalog": "__default",
            "database": "__default",
            "region": "__default"
          },
          "rawSQL": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS failed_steps FROM cloudpipe_metrics.step_outcomes WHERE status = 'failed' AND from_iso8601_timestamp(recorded_at) BETWEEN $__timeFrom() AND $__timeTo() AND CAST(dt AS DATE) BETWEEN CAST($__timeFrom() AS DATE) AND CAST($__timeTo() AS DATE)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "orange"
          }
        }
      },
      "description": "Total failed step records — larger than the participant count, since one workflow can fail several steps, and one upstream failure cascades.",
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value",
        "justifyMode": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Skipped steps",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 19,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 5,
        "h": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "cloudpipe-athena",
        "type": "grafana-athena-datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "table",
          "format": 1,
          "connectionArgs": {
            "catalog": "__default",
            "database": "__default",
            "region": "__default"
          },
          "rawSQL": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS skipped_steps FROM cloudpipe_metrics.step_outcomes WHERE status = 'skipped' AND from_iso8601_timestamp(recorded_at) BETWEEN $__timeFrom() AND $__timeTo() AND CAST(dt AS DATE) BETWEEN CAST($__timeFrom() AS DATE) AND CAST($__timeTo() AS DATE)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "blue"
          }
        }
      },
      "description": "Steps that did not need to run because their output already existed. This is the pipeline working as designed — high is good, not bad.",
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value",
        "justifyMode": "center"
      }
